          "uuid": "ff70e3c9-9591-5d3b-8264-9116792e802f",
          "stig_uuid": "20cc94ad-86d8-513a-b89a-6498204b9633",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: PostgreSQL natively logs authentication and permission/error failures, while the standard server-log path is collected by Vector. This supports existence of failure events; full actor/source/content and successful-event coverage remain explicitly flagged under database-auditing.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[pg-logging] pg-logging\nPostgreSQL18 defaults connection logging disabled and disconnection logging off; failed authentication is always logged. stderr is the default server-log destination.\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-logging.html\n\n[app-db-values] app-db-values\nDB runs under UID70 with non-root/read-only/no-escalation and dedicated PGDATA PVC; default replica count is one. Only pgaudit preload is configured, not event classes.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-postgres/values.yaml\n\n[core-vector] core-vector\nVector Agent collects Kubernetes pod and node log files, labels namespace/container/host, uses acknowledged disk buffers, and ships continuously to Loki; metrics are exported.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/vector/values/values.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. PostgreSQL natively logs authentication and permission/error failures, while the standard server-log path is collected by Vector. This supports existence of failure events; full actor/source/content and successful-event coverage remain explicitly flagged under database-auditing.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
