          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Workload/node identity labels from Vector identify the emitting PostgreSQL component/location; application audit rows also bind tenant/object context. This meets component-location context without requiring database-local duplication of every collector field.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain this source and delivered-release mapping with the component checklist; confirm applicability and accepted inheritance at sign-off.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-database-vector] re-database-vector\nVector offloads container/node logs with workload labels to centralized Loki. Collection preserves emitted records; it does not create absent successful SQL events.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/vector/values/values.yaml\n\n[re-database-permission-audit] re-database-permission-audit\nAppend-only role-change records carry tenant, individual actor/subject, grant/revoke action and timestamp; database-specific admin auditing remains distinct.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/packages/database/schema/permission_audit.pg.hcl\n\n[re-database-flag-audit] re-database-flag-audit\nSecurity-definer feature flag audit triggers record actor from app.user_id, action/old/new values and reason; demonstrates application/database-trigger auditing can meet a defined event requirement without pgAudit for that event.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/packages/database/schema/feature_flag_functions.pg.hcl",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Workload/node identity labels from Vector identify the emitting PostgreSQL component/location; application audit rows also bind tenant/object context. This meets component-location context without requiring database-local duplication of every collector field.\n\nNext action: Retain this source and delivered-release mapping with the component checklist; confirm applicability and accepted inheritance at sign-off."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-206531",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-206531",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000098",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-206531",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000098",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-206531r960900_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-206531r960900",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000098-DB-000042",
          "rule_title": "The DBMS must produce audit records containing sufficient information to establish the sources (origins) of the events.",
          "fix_text": "Configure DBMS audit settings to include the source of the event as part of the audit record.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Check DBMS settings and existing audit records to verify information specific to the source (origin) of the event is being captured and stored with audit records.\n\nIf audit records exist without information regarding the source of the event, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Database_Generic_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Information system auditing capability is critical for accurate forensic analysis. Without establishing the source of the event, it is impossible to establish, correlate, and investigate the events relating to an incident.\n\nIn order to compile an accurate risk assessment and provide forensic analysis, it is essential for security personnel to know where events occurred, such as application components, modules, session identifiers, filenames, host names, and functionality. \n\nIn addition to logging where events occur within the application, the application must also produce audit records that identify the application itself as the source of the event.\n\nAssociating information about the source of the event within the application provides a means of investigating an attack; recognizing resource utilization or capacity thresholds; or identifying an improperly configured application.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-42708",
            "V-32371"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000133"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2902",
          "uuid": "4a11a885-81f0-5501-a2e5-71e7ec7cc11c",
          "stig_uuid": "20cc94ad-86d8-513a-b89a-6498204b9633",
          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Collector labels identify the DB container but do not identify every original native SQL caller. Default native prefix is not configured with complete user/database/remote/session context; application actor-aware records cover only selected actions. Complete native audit origin/identity context is still missing for required DB/admin operations.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Configure required native session/user/database/remote context and correlate application actor where shared service roles are used.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-database-postgres-values] re-database-postgres-values\nPostgres chart args preload pgaudit and disable JIT; no pgaudit.log, native connection/disconnection logging, full log prefix, password policy hooks, session disconnect policy or encryption StorageClass selected. PVC uses host default StorageClass.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/values/postgres.yaml\n\n[re-database-pg-log] re-database-pg-log\nPostgreSQL emits server errors to stderr by default; ERROR severity identifies failed/denied SQL and log_min_error_statement includes the failing command. Successful connection/disconnection logging requires explicit settings.\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-logging.html\n\n[re-database-cls] re-database-cls\nAuthenticated tenant and user are set transaction-locally as app.tenant_id/app.user_id. Pool reuse does not retain another request identity.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/apps/api/src/core/cls/cls.adapter.ts\n\n[re-database-permission-audit] re-database-permission-audit\nAppend-only role-change records carry tenant, individual actor/subject, grant/revoke action and timestamp; database-specific admin auditing remains distinct.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/packages/database/schema/permission_audit.pg.hcl\n\n[re-database-actual-image] re-database-actual-image\nStatic export of exact delivered PostgreSQL image confirms inherited entrypoint has no audit override, PostgreSQL18 sample defaults connection logging empty/disconnections off/prefix timestampPID; actual image has FIPS provider and enabled OpenSSL configuration. File hashes and SBOM details preserved in database-image-inspection.json.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685",
          "finding_details": "Collector labels identify the DB container but do not identify every original native SQL caller. Default native prefix is not configured with complete user/database/remote/session context; application actor-aware records cover only selected actions. Complete native audit origin/identity context is still missing for required DB/admin operations.\n\nNext action: Configure required native session/user/database/remote context and correlate application actor where shared service roles are used."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-206532",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-206532",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000099",
