          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs N/A justification\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Selected PostgreSQL uses native password/service roles, not certificate-to-DB-user authentication. Mesh workload certificates protect transport and are not PostgreSQL PKI user mapping. Document the official PKI-based-authentication applicability boundary rather than configuring an unused DB certificate login.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain approved password-authentication/mesh architecture and rule-specific applicability; reassess if native DB PKI is introduced.\n\nEvidence:\n[app-db-identity] app-db-identity\nSeparate admin, horizon_app and openfga_app credentials exist. Bundled Keycloak is configured to connect using the admin DB role, a least-privilege candidate gap.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/manifests/secrets.yaml\n\n[mesh] Mesh and policy\nPackage chart declares ambient mesh and generated network policy. Disabled chart-local NetworkPolicy and plaintext application URLs do not establish missing mesh enforcement.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-uds-package/templates/package.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Needs N/A justification. Selected PostgreSQL uses native password/service roles, not certificate-to-DB-user authentication. Mesh workload certificates protect transport and are not PostgreSQL PKI user mapping. Document the official PKI-based-authentication applicability boundary rather than configuring an unused DB certificate login.\n\nNext action: Retain approved password-authentication/mesh architecture and rule-specific applicability; reassess if native DB PKI is introduced."
