        {
          "group_id_src": "V-206598",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-206598",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000381",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-206598",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000381",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-206598r981958_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-206598r981958",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000381-DB-000361",
          "rule_title": "The DBMS must produce audit records of its enforcement of access restrictions associated with changes to the configuration of the DBMS or database(s).",
          "fix_text": "Deploy a DBMS capable of producing the required audit records when it denies or fails to complete attempts to change the configuration of the DBMS or database(s).\n\nConfigure the DBMS to produce audit records when it denies attempts to change the configuration of the DBMS or database(s).\n\nConfigure the DBMS to produce audit records when other errors prevent attempts to change the configuration of the DBMS or database(s).",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Review DBMS documentation to verify audit records can be produced when the system denies or fails to complete attempts to change the configuration of the DBMS or database(s).\n\nIf the DBMS is not capable of this, this is a finding.\n\nReview the DBMS/database security and audit configurations to verify that audit records are produced when the system denies attempts to change the configuration of the DBMS or database(s).\n\nIf they are not produced, this is a finding.\n\nReview the DBMS/database security and audit configurations to verify that audit records are produced when other errors prevent attempts to change the configuration of the DBMS or database(s).\n\nIf they are not produced, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Database_Generic_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Without auditing the enforcement of access restrictions against changes to configuration, it would be difficult to identify attempted attacks and an audit trail would not be available for forensic investigation for after-the-fact actions. \n\nEnforcement actions are the methods or mechanisms used to prevent unauthorized changes to configuration settings. Enforcement action methods may be as simple as denying access to a file based on the application of file permissions (access restriction). Audit items may consist of lists of actions blocked by access restrictions or changes identified after the fact.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-72557",
            "V-58127"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-003938"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2902",
          "uuid": "e987f9af-c938-587b-a615-0e023051ad77",
          "stig_uuid": "20cc94ad-86d8-513a-b89a-6498204b9633",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: PostgreSQL logs denied/failed configuration commands through native ERROR logging and failing-statement reporting by default; Vector collects the resulting stderr.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain native error logging plus collector mapping; source context improvements remain under the separate audit-context control.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-database-pg-log] re-database-pg-log\nPostgreSQL emits server errors to stderr by default; ERROR severity identifies failed/denied SQL and log_min_error_statement includes the failing command. Successful connection/disconnection logging requires explicit settings.\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-logging.html\n\n[re-database-postgres-values] re-database-postgres-values\nPostgres chart args preload pgaudit and disable JIT; no pgaudit.log, native connection/disconnection logging, full log prefix, password policy hooks, session disconnect policy or encryption StorageClass selected. PVC uses host default StorageClass.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/values/postgres.yaml\n\n[re-database-vector] re-database-vector\nVector offloads container/node logs with workload labels to centralized Loki. Collection preserves emitted records; it does not create absent successful SQL events.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/vector/values/values.yaml\n\n[re-database-actual-image] re-database-actual-image\nStatic export of exact delivered PostgreSQL image confirms inherited entrypoint has no audit override, PostgreSQL18 sample defaults connection logging empty/disconnections off/prefix timestampPID; actual image has FIPS provider and enabled OpenSSL configuration. File hashes and SBOM details preserved in database-image-inspection.json.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. PostgreSQL logs denied/failed configuration commands through native ERROR logging and failing-statement reporting by default; Vector collects the resulting stderr.\n\nNext action: Retain native error logging plus collector mapping; source context improvements remain under the separate audit-context control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-206599",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-206599",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000383",
