          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The delivered code preloads pgAudit but does not select session event classes or enable successful native connection/disconnection records. Vector centralizes emitted logs; optional SQL tracing defaults off and cannot account for direct administrator connections. Therefore the specific required native DB event coverage remains a real shared configuration gap, despite existing product-level audit mechanisms.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Enable the required native connection/disconnection/privileged/direct-access event selection and contextual fields, with data/performance/redaction review; one shared audit workstream covers these rows.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-database-postgres-values] re-database-postgres-values\nPostgres chart args preload pgaudit and disable JIT; no pgaudit.log, native connection/disconnection logging, full log prefix, password policy hooks, session disconnect policy or encryption StorageClass selected. PVC uses host default StorageClass.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/values/postgres.yaml\n\n[re-database-extension] re-database-extension\nMigration creates pgAudit extension but catches unavailable errors; no session/object audit event settings are enabled by this migration.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/packages/database/migrations/00000000000002_create_extensions.sql\n\n[re-database-tracing] re-database-tracing\nOptional SQL tracing carries parameterized query identity, db.namespace and outcome, excluding bind values. Config def