          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000172"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2902",
          "uuid": "ff432dea-07f4-574c-a1cb-822c8e91726b",
          "stig_uuid": "20cc94ad-86d8-513a-b89a-6498204b9633",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The check first requires audit capability, then configuration for objects/actions actually selected by the owner. Shipped pgAudit supports selection of privilege/catalog reads and object access; no specific owner-selected object list was established. Do not invent an enabled-all-SQL requirement or duplicate generic event gaps.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Document selected objects/actions; enable applicable pgAudit classes/object policy under the shared database-auditing workstream if the owner requires them.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-database-extension] re-database-extension\nMigration creates pgAudit extension but catches unavailable errors; no session/object audit event settings are enabled by this migration.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/packages/database/migrations/00000000000002_create_extensions.sql\n\n[re-database-pgaudit] re-database-pgaudit\npgAudit supports selectable session/object events and role/DDL/read/write classes; preloading/extension creation alone does not select classes. Default session audit setting is none.\nhttps://github.com/pgaudit/pgaudit/blob/REL_18_STABLE/README.md",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. The check first requires audit capability, then configuration for objects/actions actually selected by the owner. Shipped pgAudit supports selection of privilege/catalog reads and object access; no specific owner-selected object list was established. Do not invent an enabled-all-SQL requirement or duplicate generic event gaps.\n\nNext action: Document selected objects/actions; enable applicable pgAudit classes/object policy under the shared database-auditing workstream if the owner requires them."
        },
