 definition.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/compose.yml\n\n[re-images-pg-sbom] re-images-pg-sbom\nActual selected PostgreSQL build source9d3725b/run41699186459 SBOM contains postgresql18.6-r7, NIST-CMVP-5132, OpenSSL FIPS provider3.4.0-r5 and fipshardened configuration. The multistage extension copy deliberately excludes/reuses runtime libcrypto/libssl, preserving base module. Release verifies selected PostgreSQL definition/context hashes and exact platform digest3431665e....\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/actions/runs/41699186459/artifacts/13263507123\n\n[re-images-vendor] re-images-vendor\nVendor documents FIPS images configured in approved-only mode; using these images is concrete enabled configuration, not an unconfigured capability. FIPS apps do not require host kernel FIPS because validated user-space entropy is included.\nhttps://www.chainguard.dev/docs/platform/fips/faqs\n\n[re-images-nist5132] re-images-nist5132\nNIST lists Chainguard FIPS Provider for OpenSSL, FIPS140-3 certificate5132, Active, sunset2031-01-13, approved-mode caveat. Exact API/web/Postgres SBOM markers map to this certificate; no certificate number guessed from generic FIPS naming.\nhttps://csrc.nist.gov/projects/cryptographic-module-validation-program/certificate/5132",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Exact selected PostgreSQL image provenance and actual build SBOM identify PostgreSQL18.6-r7, CMVP5132 OpenSSL3.4.0-r5 and approved-only fipshardened configuration. Custom extension staging preserves runtime libcrypto/libssl instead of replacing them. This resolves DBMS cryptographic-module selection for its crypto/signature/hash/confidentiality operations; it does not assert that an unspecified PVC backend has encryption enabled or that the DBMS implements an application signing workflow.\n\nNext action: Retain the exact DB image/module certificate mapping; handle backend at-rest encryption selection and any unused signing-function applicability in the separate storage/component assessment."
