          ],
          "group_id": "V-263602",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000700",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-263602r982479_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-263602r982479",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000700-DB-000100",
          "rule_title": "The DBMS must disable accounts when the accounts have expired.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the DBMS to disable accounts when the accounts have expired.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify the DBMS is configured to disable accounts when the accounts have expired.\n\nIf the DBMS is not configured to disable accounts when the accounts have expired, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Database_Generic_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Disabling expired, inactive, or otherwise anomalous accounts supports the concepts of least privilege and least functionality, which reduce the attack surface of the system.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-003627"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2902",
          "uuid": "f5758e86-ff07-5085-ba6a-dc99a6733ece",
          "stig_uuid": "20cc94ad-86d8-513a-b89a-6498204b9633",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs N/A justification\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The package provisions stable noninteractive service identities tied to workloads, not human SQL accounts whose employment or temporary access expires. Shared UDS owns human lifecycle. Native expiry/departure checks need an accepted service-account boundary and credential decommission/rotation procedure, not automatic deletion of live application roles after an individual user departure.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Record service-account owner/lifetime/decommission policy; assess any separately introduced human SQL accounts against native disablement requirements.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-database-release] re-database-release\nSuccessful UDS push42114745685 packages2026.45.4-uds.1; platform-contract selects shared UDS identity/Core1.14.0, no bundled Keycloak image. Build-info identifies appb84b9af/build19710 and Postgres digest3431665ea7f0c2dfe4bef9673aac6221a58bdf910251857123b7fb363cbb030e from source9d3725b0/run41699186459.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-database-machine-secrets] re-database-machine-secrets\nService/admin DB passwords generated with openssl rand -hex24 when not supplied, retained from existing Secrets on upgrade; app/openfga/admin are explicit deployment identities, not per-human accounts.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/zarf.yaml\n\n[re-database-role] re-database-role\nCreates/updates separate horizon_app LOGIN password role; grants DML/schema usage, no superuser or BYPASSRLS. No CONNECTION LIMIT, VALID UNTIL, password-check hook or SET ROLE escalation path.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/packages/database/migrations/00000000000003_provision_app_role.sql",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Needs N/A justification. The package provisions stable noninteractive service identities tied to workloads, not human SQL accounts whose employment or temporary access expires. Shared UDS owns human lifecycle. Native expiry/departure checks need an accepted service-account boundary and credential decommission/rotation procedure, not automatic deletion of live application roles after an individual user departure.\n\nNext action: Record service-account owner/lifetime/decommission policy; assess any separately introduced human SQL accounts against native disablement requirements."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-263603",
          "group_tree": [
