          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2902",
          "uuid": "66bd5f52-6638-5b90-b38d-92b8184f9ab1",
          "stig_uuid": "20cc94ad-86d8-513a-b89a-6498204b9633",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Whole-product approved delivery verifies real code-signing certificate identity and DSSE signatures, binds image digests inside exact packages, requires CAT vouch and publishes a digest-fixed bundle. PostgreSQL and application components are installed through that controlled immutable package path. This supplies a source-backed signed-package equivalent; lack of a second generic Pepr image-signature plugin is not by itself an application remediation finding. Acceptance of package-boundary verification versus every arbitrary cluster admission remains explicit tailoring, not a claimed universal admission policy.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain the approved package-level signer/trust mapping and restrict deployment to this verified immutable release path; assess arbitrary cluster-admin installation separately.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-images-release] re-images-release\nSuccessful Nov5 trusted release2026.45.4-uds.1 binds Horizonb84b9af/build19710/run42109769948, package d528b7f, Core1.14.0, actual identity.mode=uds issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds. Twelve delivered image platform digests are explicit; no bundled Keycloak is shipped. Published package digest sha256:486f55939f94ab081d2a12ecade5439512f8f7c4b3119c40b027c711d386adc9. Read build-info/platform-contract/publication metadata artifact13464284834, not just example chart defaults.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-images-verify] re-images-verify\nReal signer verification uses pinned DU Fulcio/Sigstore TSA anchors, expected subject/SAN/issuer, P256/SHA256 DSSE signature, code-signing EKU and RFC3161 timestamp. release.py check_evidence calls verify_production for all required phases and binds exact archives/build-info/packed image digests; CAT vouch gates publication. Actual delivery run succeeded these gates.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/scripts/ci/verify_attestation.py\n\n[re-images-publish] re-images-publish\nThe main-only protected release workflow selects qualified successful main source, validates image inventory/source digests against packed OCI manifests, binds archive SHA256SUMS, requires cryptographically verified Witness evidence and CAT vouch before registry publication; digest-qualified registry bundle fixes installation content.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/scripts/ci/release.py",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Whole-product approved delivery verifies real code-signing certificate identity and DSSE signatures, binds image digests inside exact packages, requires CAT vouch and publishes a digest-fixed bundle. PostgreSQL and application components are installed through that controlled immutable package path. This supplies a source-backed signed-package equivalent; lack of a second generic Pepr image-signature plugin is not by itself an application remediation finding. Acceptance of package-boundary verification versus every arbitrary cluster admission remains explicit tailoring, not a claimed universal admission policy.\n\nNext action: Retain the approved package-level signer/trust mapping and restrict deployment to this verified immutable release path; assess arbitrary cluster-admin installation separately."
        },
