          "reference_identifier": "2902",
          "uuid": "617eafe1-b506-5911-8c89-25681ccfb6ed",
          "stig_uuid": "20cc94ad-86d8-513a-b89a-6498204b9633",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Humans enter the product through individually authenticated shared UDS/OIDC identities; API transaction context carries their individual user and tenant before using the shared service DB role. The database is not a public shared-login service. Privileged MPN operator access remains a distinct inherited control, rather than requiring every product user to have a SQL account.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain the individual identity-to-service role context mapping and privileged operator access inheritance.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-database-release] re-database-release\nSuccessful UDS push42114745685 packages2026.45.4-uds.1; platform-contract selects shared UDS identity/Core1.14.0, no bundled Keycloak image. Build-info identifies appb84b9af/build19710 and Postgres digest3431665ea7f0c2dfe4bef9673aac6221a58bdf910251857123b7fb363cbb030e from source9d3725b0/run41699186459.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-database-cls] re-database-cls\nAuthenticated tenant and user are set transaction-locally as app.tenant_id/app.user_id. Pool reuse does not retain another request identity.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/apps/api/src/core/cls/cls.adapter.ts\n\n[re-database-role] re-database-role\nCreates/updates separate horizon_app LOGIN password role; grants DML/schema usage, no superuser or BYPASSRLS. No CONNECTION LIMIT, VALID UNTIL, password-check hook or SET ROLE escalation path.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/packages/database/migrations/00000000000003_provision_app_role.sql\n\n[re-database-package-network] re-database-package-network\nUDS ambient mesh enrolls horizon namespace and controls SQL connectivity through namespace policy. Public exposes API/web/NATS and bundledKeycloak only when selected; no public PostgreSQL endpoint.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-uds-package/templates/package.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Humans enter the product through individually authenticated shared UDS/OIDC identities; API transaction context carries their individual user and tenant before using the shared service DB role. The database is not a public shared-login service. Privileged MPN operator access remains a distinct inherited control, rather than requiring every product user to have a SQL account.\n\nNext action: Retain the individual identity-to-service role context mapping and privileged operator access inheritance."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-263608",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-263608",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000820",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-263608",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000820",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-263608r981982_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-263608r981982",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000820-DB-000170",
          "rule_title": "The DBMS must implement multifactor authentication for local; network; and/or remote access to privileged accounts; and/or nonprivileged accounts such that one of the factors is provided by a device separate from the system gaining access.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the DBMS to implement multifactor authentication for local; network; and/or remote access to privileged accounts; and/or nonprivileged accounts such that one of the factors is provided by a device separate from the system gaining access.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify the DBMS is configured to implement multifactor authentication for local; network; and/or remote access to privileged accounts; and/or nonprivileged accounts such that one of the factors is provided by a device separate from the system gaining access.\n\nIf the DBMS is not configured to implement multifactor authentication for local; network; and/or remote access to privileged accounts; and/or nonprivileged accounts such that one of the factors is provided by a device separate from the system gaining access, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Database_Generic_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "The purpose of requiring a device that is separate from the system to which the user is attempting to gain access for one of the factors during multifactor authentication is to reduce the likelihood of compromising authenticators or credentials stored on the system. Adversaries may be able to compromise such authenticators or credentials and subsequently impersonate authorized users. Implementing one of the factors on a separate device (e.g., a hardware token), provides a greater strength of mechanism and an increased level of assurance in the authentication process.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
