          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs N/A justification\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: PostgreSQL native PKI authentication/TLS trust-store functionality is not selected; password-authenticated SQL runs inside UDS ambient mutual TLS. Certificate issuance/trust is therefore assessed at the UDS mesh/gateway boundary. Do not require a second PostgreSQL trust store; attach accepted private-workload-PKI/approved-CA delegation for the actual encrypted path.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Record DB-native PKI nonapplicability and map approved trust-anchor requirements to UDS mesh/operator certificate evidence.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-database-config] re-database-config\nOpenTelemetry tracing defaults false, and SQL SSL default disabled under intended ambient mesh. No native DB certificate-auth/cache mechanism is configured.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon/blob/b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c/apps/api/src/core/config/config.schema.ts\n\n[re-database-mtls] re-database-mtls\nUDS root STRICT mesh policy authenticates/encrypts enrolled workload hops independently of PostgreSQL native TLS.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/istio/common/chart/templates/peer-authentication.yaml\n\n[re-database-package-network] re-database-package-network\nUDS ambient mesh enrolls horizon namespace and controls SQL connectivity through namespace policy. Public exposes API/web/NATS and bundledKeycloak only when selected; no public PostgreSQL endpoint.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-uds-package/templates/package.yaml\n\n[re-database-storage] re-database-storage\nUDS provisions external storage/operator services and supplied trust material; source does not identify actual MPN disk encryption settings or approved roots. Do not substitute unrelated Gallatin AWS infrastructure for MPN.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/getting-started/production/provision-services.mdx",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Needs N/A justification. PostgreSQL native PKI authentication/TLS trust-store functionality is not selected; password-authenticated SQL runs inside UDS ambient mutual TLS. Certificate issuance/trust is therefore assessed at the UDS mesh/gateway boundary. Do not require a second PostgreSQL trust store; attach accepted private-workload-PKI/approved-CA delegation for the actual encrypted path.\n\nNext action: Record DB-native PKI nonapplicability and map approved trust-anchor requirements to UDS mesh/operator certificate evidence."
        },
