          "uuid": "6db6741c-d83a-530c-b1dd-7476b9e507e7",
          "stig_uuid": "20cc94ad-86d8-513a-b89a-6498204b9633",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Gateway/mesh private keys are supplied through restricted Kubernetes Secret/identity paths, not baked into the static application image; runtime containers are non-root/read-only and platform access is separated. If an HSM is organizationally required, that additional safeguard needs an explicit requirement.\n\nComponents: Delivered PostgreSQL service accounts and application database; UDS mesh and shared identity; no bundled Keycloak database\n\nOwner: Gallatin engineering/SRE (Horizon and self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[core-gateway] core-gateway\nGateway redirects HTTP to HTTPS and requires TLS 1.3 by default, optionally TLS 1.2; credentialName references Kubernetes TLS secrets.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/istio/charts/uds-istio-config/templates/gateway.yaml\n\n[core-network] core-network\nOperator generates namespace ingress/egress default-deny NetworkPolicy; connectivity requires declared allow rules.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/pepr/operator/controllers/network/defaults/default-deny-all.ts\n\n[app-pods] app-pods\nCandidate service chart applies non-root/read-only/no-escalation contexts, Secret references, probes and resource settings. Rendered app pods corroborate those settings; some init containers lack explicit resources.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/blob/d528b7febf1ce8bb5ccf99661dade6ae09a84381/source/charts/horizon-service/templates/deployment.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Gateway/mesh private keys are supplied through restricted Kubernetes Secret/identity paths, not baked into the static application image; runtime containers are non-root/read-only and platform access is separated. If an HSM is organizationally required, that additional safeguard needs an explicit requirement.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-263621",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-263621",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000920",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-263621",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000920",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-263621r982509_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-263621r982509",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000920-DB-000320",
          "rule_title": "The DBMS must synchronize system clocks within and between systems or system components.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the DBMS to synchronize system clocks within and between systems or system components.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify the DBMS is configured to synchronize system clocks within and between systems or system components.\n\nIf the DBMS is not configured to synchronize system clocks within and between systems or system components, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Database_Generic_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Time synchronization of system clocks is essential for the correct execution of many system services, including identification and authentication processes that involve certificates and time-of-day restrictions as part of access control. Denial of service or failure to deny expired credentials may result without properly synchronized clocks within and between systems and system components. Time is commonly expressed in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC), a modern continuation of Greenwich Mean Time (GMT), or local time with an offset from UTC. The granularity of time measurements refers to the degree of synchronization between system clocks and reference clocks, such as clocks synchronizing within hundreds of milliseconds or tens of milliseconds. Organizations may define different time granularities for system components. Time service can be critical to other security capabilities such as access control and identification and authentication depending on the nature of the mechanisms used to support the capabilities.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
